# Job 029: keeps the Docker build context (repo root — see
# infra/Dockerfile's own `docker build -f infra/Dockerfile .` example)
# clean. Two distinct reasons, not just "smaller image":
#
# 1. node_modules/dist/.turbo MUST be excluded, not just "nice to skip" —
#    if the host's own locally-installed node_modules (built for whatever
#    OS/arch the dev machine is) leaked into the Linux build context,
#    `pnpm install` inside the container could see already-present
#    packages and skip reinstalling native deps (esbuild, etc.) for the
#    correct platform, producing a silently broken image that only fails
#    at runtime. A clean context forces a real, correct install every time.
# 2. .env files must NEVER reach a Docker build context — secrets baked
#    into an image layer are recoverable by anyone who can pull it, even
#    after being "removed" in a later layer. Real secrets are supplied at
#    `docker run`/the host platform's own secrets mechanism (see
#    README.md's "Production deploy" section), never copied in.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
build/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
.vite/

.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
**/.env
**/.env.local

.git/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
